 total ionization tube. More limited measurements were performed in C2H4 and SF6. Great care was taken to assure complete collection of electron and ion currents, and the absence of spurious instrumental errors. A new method was devised for obtaining absolute cross sections of gases relative to H2, and a McLeod gauge was used to obtain the absolute cross section in H2. The cross sections in NO and O2 could not be obtained by this method, and an approximate correction to direct McLeod-gauge readings was used for these gases. It is believed that the results are as accurate as is possible with the present method. It is difficult to explain the differences found between cross sections measured by various investigators. McLeod-gauge errors appear to account for most of the difference in absolute magnitude.</jats:p>","author":[{"family":"Rapp","given":"Donald","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Lockheed Missiles and Space Company, Palo Alto, California"}]},{"family":"Englander-Golden","given":"Paula","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Lockheed Missiles and Space Company, Palo Alto, California"}]}],"container-title":"The Journal of Chemical Physics","id":"temp_id_03279650425747671","issue":"5","issued":{"date-parts":[[1965,9,1]]},"language":"en","page":"1464-1479","publisher":"AIP Publishing","source":"Crossref","title":"Total Cross Sections for Ionization and Attachment in Gases by Electron Impact. I. Positive Ionization","type":"article-journal","volume":"43"},"32594577":{"DOI":"10.1103/physreva.31.2932","ISSN":"0556-2791","URL":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.31.2932","author":[{"family":"Phelps","given":"A. V.","sequence":"first"},{"family":"Pitchford","given":"L. C.","sequence":"additional"}],"container-title":"Physical Review A","container-title-short":"Phys. Rev. A","id":"temp_id_23165888464005824","issue":"5","issued":{"date-parts":[[1985,5,1]]},"language":"en","page":"2932-2949","publisher":"American Physical Society (APS)","source":"Cross